tip: | Look at the bicycle. | Almost nothing but lines. Both wheels lie on the side of an invisible box that runs along the grid, so they lean the same way as a wall.
tip: 1 | Wheels first. | Two skewed rings give the size and the direction. The frame goes between them, and its triangle is what says bicycle.
tip: 3 | Only the tires are outlined. | An outline on a 1 pixel tube fills the gaps, so the frame goes on after the outline and stands alone.
tip: 4 | Spokes are a hint. | A cross of dim pixels is enough. A full set would fill the wheel in and lose the silhouette.
